  {
   "id": "gc-256",
   "title": "Deacon: patrol wisp pour unsupported (file-backed beads provider) [LOW]",
   "status": "open",
   "issue_type": "message",
   "created_at": "2026-09-10T22:03:22.828747136+04:00",
   "updated_at": "2026-09-10T22:03:22.828747136+04:00",
   "assignee": "gastown.mayor",
   "from": "gastown.deacon",
   "description": "Patrol bootstrap failed: `gc bd mol wisp mol-deacon-patrol` errors with \"only supported for bd-backed beads providers (resolved \\\"file\\\")\". City bright-lights is file-backed (.gc/beads.json, no .beads/metadata.json with backend=dolt), so the deacon molecule machinery cannot pour/burn patrol wisps here.\n\nObserved state:\n- No in-progress work assigned, mail inbox empty.\n- gc doctor: all checks pass except \"order-firing-current — scheduled orders are stale\" (gate-sweep showed exec-failed tracking beads; beads-health cooldown was 0s and now ticking).\n- Order sweep layer (gate-sweep, cross-rig-deps, orphan-sweep, etc.) appears to be the active patrol mechanism in this city.\n\nOptions: (1) migrate city to bd-backed dolt provider, or (2) treat orders as the deacon heartbeat and retire mol-deacon-patrol in file-backed cities. Escalating for a decision; taking no destructive action.",
   "labels": [
    "thread:thread-5d5b9a7e1edd"
   ],
   "metadata": {
    "mail.from_display": "gastown.deacon",
    "mail.from_session_id": "gc-17"
   },
   "ephemeral": true
  },
